# What never reaches the build context. The Dockerfile COPYs explicitly, so this is a
# second line of defence rather than the only one — and for .env it is the line that
# matters, because a key baked into an image layer stays in that layer forever.
#
# Since D-112 the image carries no data at all, so the whole of data/ is excluded here
# rather than four directories of it. The build is a clean GitHub Actions checkout,
# which has none of it anyway; this makes a build from a developer's laptop produce the
# same image rather than a 1.2 GB one with the indexes silently baked in.

# secrets, first and always
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# every data directory: the runtime data arrives at startup as a bundle (D-112, D-114).
# This covers data/raw (109 MB of PDFs), data/processed, data/index, data/layers,
# data/gazetteer and data/logs in one line, along with the committed CSV and JSON files
# that only the pipeline scripts read.
data/

# the data bundles themselves, written by scripts/make_data_bundle.py
dist/

# local python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# node: reinstalled inside the build stage, and a host node_modules may hold binaries
# built for the wrong platform
web/node_modules/
web/dist/

# git history and tooling
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# documents and reports: for people, not for the server
docs/
reports/
*.md
!README.md

# the evaluation set: the drafts, the verified questions and every results file. The
# endpoints that read them are 404 with ZONEWISE_DEV=0 (D-075), so a public image has
# no reason to carry an unpublished question set.
eval/

# tests do not run in the image
tests/

# editor and OS litter
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
